###Step 1: Finding the length $AB$



[[☃ image 1]]

$\begin{align} 
AB^2&= {\redE{2}^2 +\redE{2}^2 }  &&\text{Pythagorean theorem}
\\\\
AB&= \sqrt{\redE{2}^2 +\redE{2}^2 }  &&\text{Square root both sides}
\\\\
&=\tealE{\sqrt{8}}
\end{align}$

We're looking for an approximate answer, so we won't try to simplify this radical. Also, let's not round until the end.

